==Trivia==
*Most of the stages' Japanese names contain confection-related puns:
**[[Crunchy Cookie Canyon|Zakuzakukkī Sanmyaku]] (ザクザクッキー山脈, "Zakuzakookie Mountains"): Pun on ザクザク ''zakuzaku'' (a "crunchy" onomatopoeia that can refer to cutting into large pieces) and クッキー ''kukkī'' (cookie).
**[[Tapioca Hills|Wasuregataki Tapi Oka]] (忘れがたきタピ丘, "Unforgettable Tapi Hill"): Pun on タピオカ ''tapioka'' ([[wikipedia:Tapioca|tapioca]]) and 丘 ''oka'' (hill).
**[[Nata de Coco Way|Hikyō Nata de Kodō]] (秘境ナタ・デ古道, "Secluded Nata de Old Road"): Pun on ''[[wikipedia:Nata de coco|nata de coco]]'' and 古道 ''kodō'' (old road).
**[[Fudge Mausoleum|Hin'yari Choko Reibyō]] (ひんやりチョコ霊廟, "Chilly Choco Mausoleum"): Pun on チョコレート ''chokorēto'' (chocolate) and 霊廟 ''reibyō'' (mausoleum).
*[[Ange Lackey]]'s projectile bears a slight resemblance to a yellow ''[[wikipedia:Konpeitō|konpeitō]]'', which may be why they debut in this confection-themed sub-chapter.
*[[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]] appearing in [[Fudge Mausoleum]] is likely a reference to his love of sweets.
*In all versions except [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], [[Creamy Snowplain]] was [[Commander Ostromeda]]'s first appearance overall, as [[Anniversary/12 1/2 Year#Arrival of the Blue Ship|Arrival of the Blue Ship]] still hadn't been released outside of Japan by the time Patisserie Parklands was added to other versions.

